    "<!--\n",
    "TODO: draft. Left intentionally blank.\n",
    "\n",
    "Elements to hit when drafting (from the project brief, not yet prose):\n",
    "  - Conjoint measures preference among alternatives the respondent was shown;\n",
    "    it is silent on what she would have looked at and what looking costs.\n",
    "  - The two-stage list-then-detail architecture is how many categories are\n",
    "    actually shopped; the instrument reproduces it.\n",
    "  - The nesting claim is load-bearing: conjoint is the zero-search-cost\n",
    "    special case of SIFT. Non-adversarial, roughly true, and testable.\n",
    "  - Two technical claims: (i) within-respondent panel of search spells\n",
    "    supports individual-level preference AND search-cost estimates;\n",
    "    (ii) exogenous variation in position and information architecture is\n",
    "    designed in rather than found.\n",
    "  - One-line version: conjoint tells you what people prefer once they are\n",
    "    looking; SIFT tells you what they look at, what it costs them to look,\n",
    "    and what they never see at all.\n",
    "  - Contributions list, then roadmap paragraph pointing at each section.\n",
    "-->"
